      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. Fifty mg of amlodipine is five times the maximum dose, and I don't know of any indication for it in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. It could cause serious harm, including profound hypotension and shock. Amlodipine's long half-life means the effects would last for days.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **If the dose was a mistake,** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right away.\n- **If the team wants more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives,** the usual step is to add another agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. Your resident or attending can choose it.\n- **If an attending wants 50 mg for a specific reason,** they should enter or co-sign the order themselves. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it too.\n\nTell me which option you'd like, and I'll enter the order."
      }
